-- title:
--   Unique infinitesimal lifting of θ-points of label (g,j)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, the data are those of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison for fake elliptic curves, in the form of an abstract point functor.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r,\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`) and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree (`hN`) and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrN`, `hrbarN`).
--
--   **Coefficients.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi\in\mathcal O$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies, modulo $\pi$, a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Finally $vdet:GL_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is the homomorphism characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion algebra and its moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB` asserting that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and that, for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$, the completion is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or above $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ a maximal order (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ via $f$, together with a point map `pt` sending a fake elliptic curve with level-$N$ structure over a ring $S$ (with a chosen $\mathcal O$-point $s$) to an $s$-point of $f$, is a coarse moduli space in the sense of `IsCoarseModuli` (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pull-back, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property).
--
--   **Full level $n$ and fine moduli.** A natural number $n\ge 3$ (`hn`) prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`); a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptF` on curves with full level-$n$ structure which is a fine moduli space (`hM`); a group $G$ with $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ forming a level-twisting action (`hρ`: $\rho$ acts over the base, twisting a level structure by $\chi(g)$ moves the point by $\rho(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$).
--
--   **Forgetful map, Hecke and Atkin–Lehner correspondences.** A morphism $M\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a coarse moduli space $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with extra level $\ell$ (`h𝒴`), with two morphisms $d_0,d_1$ to $\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and dividing by it (`hd₁`, via `IsLevelIsogeny`). Endomorphisms $ar,arbar$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner involutions at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef` asserting $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and ramification exactly at the place above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`); a finite idele $n_1\in\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,R_1\,r$ (`hn₁`) such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma t$ equal to the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ integral for $R_1$ at all places $\ne v$ (`hΓt`); families $s_\ell$ of units and $sf_\ell$ of finite ideles indexed by the primes $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ with `hs`: the component of $sf_\ell$ at a place not above $r$ is $s_\ell\otimes1$, its components above $r$ are $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in $\mathrm{levelHeckeUSet}\,\Lambda_1\,(R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})\,\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in $\mathrm{primeHeckeSet}\,(R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1})\,\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; the subgroups $\Gamma t_\ell=\Gamma t\cap s_\ell\Gamma t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Order coordinates.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$, and a map $coord:\Lambda\to \mathrm{Zp2}(r)^2$ (Witt vectors of $\mathbb F_{r^2}$) satisfying `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`): additivity, normalisation of $1$, the Frobenius-twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, density modulo all powers of $r$, and the trace identity.
--
--   **Data on the special fibre.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ over the same ring of height $4$ (`hX₀`), two-variable formal coordinates $\theta_0$ along the unit section of $A_0$, with $A_0$ a formal module via $coord$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`); endomorphisms $e_\gamma,e'_\gamma$ of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma t$, with $e_\gamma$ over the base (`he`), and exponents $\deg\gamma$. The uniformisation hypotheses on these are: `hE1` (each pair $(e_\gamma,e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level structure); `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $\gamma\mapsto e_\gamma$ up to multiplication by powers of $r$); `hE1sc` (for $\gamma$ a rational integer scalar $c$, $e_\gamma$ is multiplication by $c$ up to powers of $r$); `hE1'` (conversely, if $e_\gamma$ is a multiplication by a positive integer up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a scalar); `hE2` (for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of $\{X_0.\mathrm{actEnd}\}\cup\{X_0.\mathrm{varpiEnd}\}$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$-coordinates, in the nilpotent sense, by a centraliser element $\varepsilon$ with $E_0\varepsilon=r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$); `hE3` (each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ carries a labelling $\Gamma t\to\Lambda$, multiplicative and scalar-compatible modulo $n$, describing the action of the $e_\gamma$ on it); `hE4` (over algebraically closed fields over $Onr/(\pi)$, every $r$-power isogeny pair preserving level on a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to powers of $r$); and the hypotheses for a further order $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) together with $\hat e:R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê`): `hE5a` ($\hat e_x$ is a homomorphism for the group law, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unitality, $\hat e_{xy}=\hat e_y$ followed by $\hat e_x$, and integers act by multiplication), `hE5c` ($\hat e_{\bar x}$ followed by $\hat e_x$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$), `hE5d` (compatibility of $\hat e_x$ with $e_\gamma$ when $x=r^k\gamma$, up to powers of $r$) and `hE5e` (the joint form of `hE2` covering simultaneously the $e_\gamma$ and the $\hat e_x$ with one and the same $g$).
--
--   **Formal-module moduli package.** A ring map $\iota:\mathrm{Zp2}(r)\to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a map $\eta$ from rigidified $\Phi$-data over $B$ to $MD(B)$, whose three properties (`hη`) are: over Noetherian $B$, two admissible rigidified objects have the same image exactly when they are isomorphic; naturality under ring maps; and local surjectivity, every point of $MD(B)$ being, on a Zariski cover of $B$ by localisations, the $\eta$-image of an admissible rigidified object. An injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-actions into $M_2(K_0)$ for which some $m$ makes $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ contained in and $r^{m}$ times the image contained in $M_2(\mathcal O)$ (`hE₀`).
--
--   **Drinfeld comparison for the package.** A family of maps $eD$ from the $\mathcal O$-points functor $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal O\,MD$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega_{K_0,\pi}$, natural in the $\mathcal O$-algebra (`hnatD`), bijective on every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hbijD`), compatible with the leg (`hfstD`: the first component of $eD(x)$ is $x.\psi$), intertwining the $GL_2(K_0)$-action on package points with the $vdet$-twisted action on pairs (`hGLD`), sending $\pi$-translation to Frobenius twist of the leg with unchanged Deligne datum (`hPiD`), and such that $\pi$-translates always exist (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Transport data.** A ring map $\kappa:Onr/(\pi)\to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to $X_0$ pushed forward along $\kappa$, of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on the special fibre: a curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $aw,aw'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), and $bw,bw'$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_{0w}$ to $A_0$ preserving level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ lying over the base (`habw`), together with `hJOINTw`, the joint uniformisation statement producing one $g$ realising simultaneously the $e_\gamma$ as $g\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$ up to powers of $r$ and the composite $aw$ followed by $bw$ as $g\iota_0(\bar w)g^{-1}$ up to a power of $r$.
--
--   **The comparison functor $\Xi$.** A construction assigning to each rigidified fake elliptic curve over a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, relative to a leg $\psi:Onr\to B$, a point of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.GPoint}\,\mathcal O\,MD$ over $B$, subject to: `hΞleg` (over $B$ with only the trivial idempotents, the leg of $\Xi$ is $\psi$ twisted by some integral power of $Fr$); `hΞnat` (compatibility with pull-back of rigidified curves along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps); `hΞiso` ($\Xi$ is unchanged under an isomorphism of the underlying curves respecting the group law, the $\Lambda$-action and the level, together with a comparison of the two rigidifications up to a pair of $r$-power multiplications); `hΞdef` (over $B$ connected in the above sense with $r$ nilpotent, if the curve is a formal module via $coord$, $X$, $\theta$, then for some $j\le1$ there is an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X=X$, transporting the rigidification via $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$ with parameter $j$, and $\Xi$ of the curve equals the triple consisting of $\psi$ twisted by $Fr^{-j}$ and $\eta$ applied to $t$). An element $g_0\in GL_2(K_0)$ for which: `heqΓ` (over connected $B$, translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds to the package-level action by $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some integer $c$) and `heqW` (over connected $B$ with $\bar r$ invertible, an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, together with the stated comparison of the two rigidifications through $aw$ followed by $bw$, corresponds to the action by $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$).
--
--   **The abstract point functor and the family $\theta$.** A Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hCπ`) with a leg $\chi_C:Onr\to C$; a functor $PR$ on $C$-algebras; a point map $ptR$ which, for a $C$-algebra $S$ that is also an $\mathcal O$-algebra compatibly, and for the leg $\psi_S$ obtained from $\chi_C$ by base change, assigns to a curve with full level-$n$ structure together with a rigidification relative to $A_0$ an element of $PR(S)$. Its properties are: `hR2` (compatibility with pull-back along $C$-algebra maps, for pairs whose level structures and rigidifications correspond); `hR3s` (every element of $PR(S)$ is of this form); `hR3i` (over $S$ whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, equality of two points forces an isomorphism of the curves-with-level together with a comparison of the rigidifications up to a pair of $r$-power multiplications); `hR1` (conversely, such an isomorphism forces equality of the points). Finally a family $\theta_S:PR(S)\to\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(S)$ for Noetherian such $S$, natural in $S$ (`hθnat`), and characterised by `hθ`: $\theta_S(ptR(u,\rho))$ is the pull-back by $(g_0^{-1})^{-1}$ of the Deligne-datum component of $eD$ applied to $\Xi(u_1,\rho)$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Let $S$ be a local Artinian ring with algebraically closed residue field, Noetherian, a $C$-algebra and an $\mathcal O$-algebra with the scalar tower $\mathcal O\to C\to S$, and let $S_0$ be a nontrivial Noetherian ring with the same structures. Let $p:S\to S_0$ be a surjective $C$-algebra map (the letter $p$ here shadows the earlier morphism $M\to\mathcal X$) whose kernel has square zero, in the stated form: $ps=pt=0$ implies $st=0$. Let $g\in G$, $j\in\{0,1\}$, $x_0\in PR(S_0)$ and $d\in\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(S)$.
--
--   Assume first that $x_0$ admits a presentation of label $(g,j)$: $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S_0$, and there are a leg $\psi_{S_0}$ equal to the base change of $\chi_C$, a curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S_0$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of $u_1$ relative to $A_0$ such that $ptR(u,\rho)=x_0$; there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $u_1$ which is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\rho$ (in the sense of `IsNormLevelTransport` for $Fr,\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0,\Phi,\iota,coord$) and the given level structure $u_2.P$ is the translate of $P_n$ by the action of $\chi(g)$; and the leg of $\Xi(u_1,\rho)$ is $\psi_{S_0}$ twisted by $Fr^{-j}$. Assume moreover $\theta_{S_0}(x_0)=\Omega_{K_0,\pi}(p)(d)$, the image of $d$ under the map induced by $p$ viewed as an $\mathcal O$-algebra map.
--
--   Then there is exactly one $x\in PR(S)$ such that: (i) $x$ admits a presentation of label $(g,j)$ over $S$, that is, $\pi$ is nilpotent in $S$ and there are a leg $\psi_S$ equal to the base change of $\chi_C$, a curve with full level-$n$ structure $u$ over $S$ and a rigidification $\rho$ of $u_1$ with $ptR(u,\rho)=x$, a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $u_1$ which is the height-normalised transport of $P_0$ along $\rho$ with $u_2.P$ the translate of $P_n$ by $\chi(g)$, and the leg of $\Xi(u_1,\rho)$ equal to $\psi_S$ twisted by $Fr^{-j}$; (ii) $PR(p)(x)=x_0$; and (iii) $\theta_S(x)=d$.
--
--   This is the infinitesimal lifting and rigidity step for the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison map $\theta$ in its representability-agnostic form, stated for an abstract point functor $PR$ on $C$-algebras rather than for a representing scheme: along a square-zero surjection of Artinian base rings it says that a point of $\Omega$ over $S$ lifting a given $\theta$-value has a unique preimage of prescribed label $(g,j)$. It combines the existence statement `omega_family_exists_lift_label_of_isArtinianRing_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr` with the uniqueness statement `omega_family_eq_of_label_of_theta_eq_of_isArtinianRing_of_rigidifiedToG_connInj_pr`, and is used in the construction and uniqueness of even rigidified pairs, feeding the relative representability of rigidified fake elliptic curves over the Drinfeld upper half plane.
